    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">euphrŏne</span></b> , es,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφρόνη</span> (the
		propitious), euphemism for <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>night</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut euethen Graeci dicimus stultum, et noctem
					euphronen, et furias Eumenidas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 8, 33</span></i>
			; cf. Lidd. and Scott, s. v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐφρόνη</span>.</div>
